  "worked_solution": "The level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=-1.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\frac{z}{x-y} & =-1 \\\\ z & =y-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface for $c=-1$ is the plane $z=y-x.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
